WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.312
Raj: The replay position trails received WAL. Primary sends and B receives promptly.

2
00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:13.367
Hannah: Then received logs aren't readable data yet. Replay must apply their changes first.

3
00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:20.279
Anika: That fits the stale order samples. Read-after-write consistency fails on B currently.

4
00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:26.806
Priya: Okay, network failure looks unlikely, right? Can we rule that out entirely?

5
00:00:26.806 --> 00:00:34.270
Lukas: Not entirely, just this observed bottleneck. Current receive progress doesn't show transport stalls.

6
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:40.510
Raj: Our working hypothesis is slow apply. B's disk queue rose around nine.

7
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:47.613
Hannah: Check replay conflicts and local jobs. Disk pressure could have several causes.

8
00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:53.733
Priya: So, what's the ETA for correlation? About three minutes would be useful.

9
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:59.948
Lukas: I'll compare primary WAL generation rates. We need both sides of this.

10
00:00:59.948 --> 00:01:06.020
Anika: I'm on it for routing preparation. No live switch until capacity checks pass.

